  <div class="about-hero">
    <h1>About ByteNote</h1>
    <p>ByteNote is an independent publication covering cybersecurity research, web technology, and application security. Founded in 2019, we publish original research, practical tutorials, and in-depth analysis written by working practitioners.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="page-header" style="border-bottom:none; padding-bottom:0; margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
    <div class="page-header-eyebrow">Mission</div>
    <h1>Making Security Knowledge Accessible</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="article-body">
    <p>Web application security is a discipline where incomplete knowledge is dangerous. A developer who understands that SQL injection exists but does not understand parameterized queries will implement them incorrectly. A security engineer who knows that XSS is "about scripts" but cannot articulate the difference between HTML, attribute, JavaScript, and URL contexts will miss real vulnerabilities.</p>
    <p>ByteNote exists to close those gaps. Every article we publish is written with the goal of leaving the reader meaningfully better equipped to build or test secure software — not just aware that a problem exists.</p>

